It does not change the license of third-party materials, including upstream
Bhatti code, libkrucible/libkrun, Linux, Ubuntu packages, or bundled tools.
Their applicable licenses and notices continue to govern those materials.
See NOTICE and licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

This license is prospective. It does not revoke, narrow, or replace rights
already granted in copies or versions previously supplied under Apache-2.0
or another license. A person exercising those independently granted rights
remains subject to that earlier license, not this revenue restriction.

2. Definitions

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
license. Use in the course of employment or on behalf of an organization is
use by that organization, not separate personal use by its staff.

"Affiliate" means an entity controlling, controlled by, or under common
control with You. Control means ownership of more than 50 percent of voting
interests or the power to direct management. Your "Group" includes You and
all Affiliates. Intra-group revenue is counted only once.

"ARR" means Your Group's total worldwide annual recurring revenue from ALL
products and services, not only those using AHVM. Measure ARR at the end of
each calendar month as the annualized value of recurring subscription,
contract and service revenue then in force: multiply monthly recurring
revenue by 12 and use the annual value of annual recurring contracts. For
recurring usage-based revenue, annualize the monthly average of the last
three completed months, or all completed months if fewer than three exist.
Exclude nonrecurring charges, sales taxes, refunds and credits. Convert
non-USD amounts using a consistently applied, publicly available month-end
exchange rate. Apply these rules consistently and in good faith.

"Eligible" means Your Group's ARR does not exceed USD 1,000,000. An individual
acting solely on their own behalf with no recurring business revenue is
Eligible. Splitting operations among Affiliates does not avoid the threshold.

